From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:00:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] workspace_source v2 consumer: scratch-owned external
 worktrees and selected artifacts

Core consumer for Board source protocol 2 (hermes-hub PR #137, deployed as
8115b6dd). Squashed from the reviewed spike branch
spike/workspace-source-v2-t_0a6a9f59d9af4492 (23 commits, last 45c9a80e),
rebased onto current main. Card: t_0a6a9f59d9af4492, split from
t_473349cceeb5510a.

Inert by default: the advertised SOURCE_PROTOCOL stays 1, so no Board grant
selects protocol 2 until a later change flips the advertisement. v1 worktree
routing is unchanged.

What it adds
- Scratch `initial` attach (kanban_source_registration): a live `ready` lease
  holder registers a configured clone's external worktree via the bound
  `kanban_heartbeat(source_path=...)`. Worker guard, bound task/run, caller-run
  check, N6 lane check (Board authoritative) and in-transaction rechecks. No
  terminal Kanban-mutation exception.
- Repository identity (id, full_name, common-dir, kind) persisted on
  observations; published v2 attach and every ending re-prove it. Exact
  full_name stays fail-closed on rename (retains custody, loses nothing).
- Selected artifacts: explicit selection via heartbeat `artifacts` or the
  completion/review surface; durable no-follow snapshots with descriptor
  identity checks, sha256 dedup, task_attachments + existing blob transport,
  successor inheritance only after exact predecessor proof, launch-time
  download and sha256 verification.
- Publication/receipt fences: live run and selection rechecked around the
  manifest RPC; stale portable receipts downgraded to retained inside the
  ending transaction; move rolls back on a stale receipt.
- Ending origin proof bound to the shared preflight deadline and run once;
  artifact metadata/blob I/O share the same budget with a transfer watchdog.
- M3: refusal codes split into definite (nothing attached) and uncertain;
  pending rows are compare-and-deleted / CAS'd, never blindly erased.
- Move/reclaim gates honour scratch custody (a scratch card with an external
  worktree publishes before a running move; reclaim refuses source custody);
  the holder finds its own run after an unchanged ending.
- Docs: kanban.md "Scratch cards that edit a repository (source protocol 2)"
  and docs/workspace-source-v2-*.md.

Rebase notes
- hermes_cli/kanban_metadata_files.py conflicted with main's
  kanban_artifact_receipt.record_files rewrite. Resolution: selected-snapshot
  mapping (completion_mapping) is passed to record_files as `relocated`, so a
  receipt/metadata reference to an original path reuses the snapshot instead
  of copying bytes changed after the snapshot (caught by
  test_kanban_source_completion_stage RED after the first resolution).
- Two new test files imported shared fixtures by name (F811 under main's
  health ratchet); switched to module attribute bindings.

Verification
- 34 source suites + workspace_source: all green on this head.
- Regression: every test file referencing the touched modules (408 files).
- scripts/check --base origin/main.
- Spike evidence (Board+core composed HTTP proofs incl. managed dispatch,
  27 controls; condition mutants) lives in daveey/hermes-hub
  docs/spikes/workspace-source-v2/ on the spike branch.
